WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.355 --> 00:00:07.769
Tom Lindqvist: Hey Vanessa, Darnell. How's the weather down in Tampa today?

2
00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:18.864
Vanessa Grant: Hot. I mean, it's September in Florida, so... you know how it goes. Ninety-four degrees and it rained sideways for ten minutes at lunch.

3
00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:26.500
Darnell Wright: I got caught in that walking back from the parking garage. Um, Looked like I'd been swimming.

4
00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:34.042
Tom Lindqvist: Ha. Uh, well, I'm sorry. I'm up in Portland, it's sixty-two and drizzling, so we're even.

5
00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:38.714
Vanessa Grant: Okay, so, agenda. You sent a couple of things over.

6
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:50.160
Tom Lindqvist: Yeah. I mostly wanted to check in on the voice agent numbers and whatever Darnell's got running, and then look at where we are before the fall push.

7
00:00:51.215 --> 00:01:00.053
Darnell Wright: Before we get into that, one thing I want to put on I mean, the record, because I've been meaning to send it up to you you.

8
00:01:01.215 --> 00:01:02.015
Tom Lindqvist: Go ahead.

9
00:01:02.721 --> 00:01:14.188
Darnell Wright: So, our website's one of those single-page apps, right? When somebody taps a phone number on a showroom page, the page doesn't do a full reload, it swaps the content underneath.

10
00:01:14.188 --> 00:01:18.257
Darnell Wright: And what we're seeing is the number doesn't swap with it.

11
00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:23.377
Tom Lindqvist: Meaning the dynamic number insertion isn't firing on the route change.

12
00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:36.475
Darnell Wright: Right. So a customer on the mobile site, they click to call, and they're getting the default number, not the one tied to whatever page or campaign brought them in.

13
00:01:36.475 --> 00:01:42.950
Darnell Wright: It's not every call, but it's enough that I don't trust the attribution on mobile anymore.

14
00:01:44.023 --> 00:01:48.906
Tom Lindqvist: I mean, okay. How long do you figure this has been going on?

15
00:01:49.835 --> 00:02:03.176
Darnell Wright: Honestly? Probably since the site rebuild over the like, summer. Nobody flagged it until my team lead on the queue started comparing call logs to the ad reports and the numbers didn't line up.

16
00:02:04.011 --> 00:02:14.352
Vanessa Grant: And I care about so, this because if mobile click-to-call isn't attributing, then Google Ads is getting fed garbage, and I'm making budget calls off garbage.

17
00:02:15.022 --> 00:02:25.528
Tom Lindqvist: No, that makes sense. Let me ask a couple of things so I can describe it accurately when I bring it to to the team.

18
00:02:25.528 --> 00:02:31.412
Tom Lindqvist: Is it happening on both iOS and Android, or did you only test one?

19
00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:44.420
Darnell Wright: We saw it on both. My analyst pulled a sample last week, I want to say around nine hundred mobile sessions, and about forty of them showed the wrong number in the source.

20
00:02:45.587 --> 00:02:51.778
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. And is it just the showroom pages or also the campaign landing pages?

21
00:02:52.527 --> 00:02:59.175
Darnell Wright: Both, I think. The landing pages are simpler so it's harder to to catch, but yeah.

22
00:02:59.948 --> 00:03:15.629
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. I'm not going to guess at what's behind it. Let me write it up with those details and get it in front of the right folks, and I'll come back to you with questions rather than a theory.

23
00:03:16.011 --> 00:03:22.299
Darnell Wright: That's you know, all I'm asking. Put it in writing so I've got something to point at.

24
00:03:23.306 --> 00:03:28.375
Tom Lindqvist: Will do. Okay, other side of the house. How's the voice agent doing?

25
00:03:28.594 --> 00:03:35.463
Darnell Wright: Good. It's handling store hours and order status, those two intents, and it's taking a real bite out of the queue.

26
00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.170
Vanessa Grant: Last month it was, what, about a third of inbound?

27
00:03:40.839 --> 00:03:45.675
Darnell Wright: Thirty-four percent, yeah. And on Sundays it's higher because we run lean.

28
00:03:46.246 --> 00:03:51.062
Tom Lindqvist: And the transfers to live agents, are those landing where you want them?

29
00:03:51.494 --> 00:04:02.602
Darnell Wright: They are. Amazon Connect's been solid. Had to move one supervisor to a later shift because the call curve shifted, but that's a staffing thing, not a system thing.

30
00:04:03.191 --> 00:04:06.171
Vanessa Grant: Speak for yourself, I'm still fighting for that headcount.

31
00:04:06.607 --> 00:04:08.473
Darnell Wright: You and me um, both.

32
00:04:08.723 --> 00:04:13.483
Tom Lindqvist: Anything else that's come up that you want me to carry back?

33
00:04:14.292 --> 00:04:20.419
Darnell Wright: No. Everything else we're running is fine. This is the one that's bugging me.

34
00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:27.192
Vanessa Grant: Same. We're heads down on Q4, so I don't have bandwidth for a project right now anyway.

35
00:04:27.706 --> 00:04:35.556
Tom Lindqvist: Understood. So what I'll do, I'll get the write-up together today or tomorrow, and copy you both so you can add anything I missed.

36
00:04:36.732 --> 00:04:40.838
Vanessa Grant: I mean, Perfect. And when do you want to talk again?

37
00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:48.193
Tom Lindqvist: How about two weeks, same time? That gives me room to come back with something real.

38
00:04:49.062 --> 00:04:56.458
Darnell Wright: Works for me. I'll have my analyst pull a fresh sample before then so we're comparing apples to apples.

39
00:04:57.931 --> 00:05:03.222
Tom Lindqvist: That'd help. Send it over whenever, you don't need to wait for the meeting.

40
00:05:04.217 --> 00:05:07.897
Darnell Wright: Will do. Alright, I mean, I've got a one-on-one in five.

41
00:05:09.025 --> 00:05:12.252
Vanessa Grant: Yeah, I need to run too. Thanks, Tom.

42
00:05:13.086 --> 00:05:15.098
Tom Lindqvist: Thanks both. Stay dry, Darnell.

43
00:05:15.907 --> 00:05:17.399
Darnell Wright: I mean, no promises.
